oker. Notice that if the pair of 2s is split into singles, there are exactly three high control cards (2, 2, Red Joker) to cover the three weak singles (4, 6, Q). This creates a perfect "kicker" strategy where you play a low single, regain the lead with a high card, and repeat, eventually finishing with the pair of 5s. Leading the pair of 5s is risky as it removes your only small pair and forces you to rely on 22 immediately if a pair is returned, potentially stranding your singles.\n\nReason: Leading the lowest single (♥4) is the optimal strategy. It initiates the plan to clear the "trash" singles (4, 6, Q) while holding the strong control cards (2, 2, Red Joker) to regain the lead. This approach keeps the pair of 2s flexible—they can be used as a powerful pair if the opponents shift to pairs, or split to dominate single rounds.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♥4"]}'}
